ked unhealthy. Rolled back all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. After the rollback, the service reports healthy with a 0.2% error rate. Next step: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 52170, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_0148ExQiHsrFiPYjyFjyZNhY", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 52170, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_0148ExQiHsrFiPYjyFjyZNhY", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 55961, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release. Both later releases, v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1, were marked unhealthy. All three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) now run v2.3.0. The error rate dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The first request to open the incident timed out. I checked and found it hadn't been created, so I sent it again with the same idempotency key. That key prevents a duplicate, so only INC-0001 exists. It records the failing v2.3.1 deploy, the rollback to v2.3.0, the recovery numbers, and a follow-up to find what broke in v2.3.1 before redeploying.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01AmhN1YyVVsyaTzPSBiQp21", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01CHqdZnqMCJzFuwQj9Lba4M", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent healthy release is v2.3.0 (seq 1). The later releases, v2.3.1-rc (seq 2) and v2.3.1 (seq 3), are both unhealthy. Rolling back now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_012K2QSsTfJmJUpS49yPGrdV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01DKmrTTaw1RbuVr9KnHr23F", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_014HY9onvibNd9ik1TeTQezW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01YLxGpEAmqEUKAS2Muuqrww", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy \u2014 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of 18%. The previous candidate v2.3.1-rc was also marked unhealthy. Rolled back all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. After the rollback, the service reports healthy with a 0.2% error rate. Next step: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01N5de47jgkT4iJCJxztXAvY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The incident wasn't created, so I'm retrying with the same idempotency key, which prevents a duplicate.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_0148ExQiHsrFiPYjyFjyZNhY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy \u2014 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of 18%. The previous candidate v2.3.1-rc was also marked unhealthy. Rolled back all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. After the rollback, the service reports healthy with a 0.2% error rate. Next step: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release. Both later releases, v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1, were marked unhealthy. All three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) now run v2.3.0. The error rate dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The first request to open the incident timed out. I checked and found it hadn't been created, so I sent it again with the same idempotency key. That key prevents a duplicate, so only INC-0001 exists. It records the failing v2.3.1 deploy, the rollback to v2.3.0, the recovery numbers, and a follow-up to find what broke in v2.3.1 before redeploying.", "type": "text"}]}]}